<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh taka ends flat against dollar.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh taka ends flat against dollar.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bangladesh taka recovered from an early fall to close flat at 43.7600/7700 to the dollar in interbank trading on Wednesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The local unit was quoted weaker at 43.7600/7900 per dollar in early trade but recovered by midday as demand for the U.S. currency eased slightly.</p>
<p>Interbank call money rates closed unchanged at 7.5 to 8.5 percent, dealers said.</p>
<p>- Dhaka Newsroom +880-2-506363</p>
